  "$description": "The machine form of frontiers-written-voice's rules (spec FR-008 to FR-013 and FR-021): what sweep.py looks for. Matching ignores case and treats curly quotes as straight. A phrase of one word in hedges or throat_clearing warns; a longer one fails. spec.md is the source; this file must agree with it. The headline lists are for headings and titles: a heading that starts with a word in fail_headline_starts, or is one of fail_headline_labels, announces a topic or an activity instead of stating the claim (FR-009); one that starts with a phrase in warn_headline_starts names a topic and is read again by a person. The fail_self_description list holds regular expressions, matched ignoring case: prose that describes the page's own apparatus, what its items, cards or sections say, show or carry, and how they are arranged (FR-009).",
